0198: GPU DCVS on its own thread, with an input boost, on by default

Since 0189 iOS draws through user submits (0153), so 0151's DCVS tick,
called at the end of a kernel present, never ran: the GPU stayed at
bluegpu_mhz (710 MHz) for the whole boot. A kernel thread now ticks
every 100 ms with the ring lock held (rs_recover takes it too); the
present-path tick only runs without the thread.

Input boost: SweetHID calls blue_gpu_core_input() on every touch event
and key. For bluegpu_dcvs_boost_ms (1000) after one, the level is at
least bluegpu_dcvs_boost (520 MHz); the thread is woken at once when
the clock is below it. Without it, animations started by a touch began
at 257 MHz and lost frames (p90 frame gaps 44-60 ms against 37 ms at
710 MHz, tools/framegaps.py). The busy target is 50% (was 65).

blueui now includes bluegpu_dcvs=1 (bluegpu_dcvs=0 fixes the clock at
bluegpu_mhz again). Log: the first 20 level changes, then one in 100;
every 10 s one line with busy %, the level, changes, boosts and the
time spent at each level.

